WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:07.760
The Lagoon Nebula is a giant emission nebula with an H II region located in the constellation Sagittarius.

00:08.276 --> 00:18.095
Discovered by Giovanni Hodierna in 1654, it is one of only two star-forming nebulae faintly visible to the naked eye from mid-northern latitudes.
